  "worked_solution": "The inequality $x<-5$ or $x>-3$ means that $x$ can take any value less than $-5,$ or greater than $-3.$\n\nTo represent this on a number line, we graph the two separate inequalities:\n\n- the inequality $x<-5$ consists of an open circle at $-5$ and an arrow to the left.\n\n- the inequality $x>-3$ consists of a open circle at $-3$ and an arrow to the right.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](@asset-0@)",
